   "quote": "capitis aurei genialem caesariem ambrosia temulentam",
   "trans": "the delightful hair of his golden head, dripping with ambrosia",
   "body": "The blazon of Cupid opens with his hair: <em>aureum caput</em> (\"golden head\"), the <em>genialis caesaries</em> (\"delightful locks\") and <em>ambrosia temulenta</em> — \"drunk/soaked with ambrosia\". The divine perfume and golden gleam mark him at once as a god.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"The richly sensuous description — golden hair <em>ambrosia temulentam</em> (‘dripping with ambrosia’) — establishes Cupid’s divinity through sight and smell, and explains Psyche’s helpless wonder.\"",
   "line": ""
  },
