   "label": "Coinage & Antithesis",
   "quote": "alios antependulos, alios retropendulos",
   "trans": "some hanging in front, others hanging behind",
   "body": "Apuleius coins a matched pair of compound adjectives — <em>ante-pendulos</em> and <em>retro-pendulos</em> (\"fore-hanging\" / \"back-hanging\") — set in neat antithesis (<em>alios ... alios</em>). The invented words are part of his showy, novel style.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"The coined, antithetical compounds <em>antependulos ... retropendulos</em> show Apuleius’s playful, mannered style; the balanced <em>alios ... alios</em> lets the eye travel over Cupid’s tumbling curls.\"",
   "line": ""
  },
