   "body": "Cupid’s radiance is so great (<em>splendore nimio fulgurante</em>) that the lamp’s own flame <em>vacillabat</em> — wavers, as if dazzled. The light that exposed him is itself outshone.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"Hyperbole and personification combine: the god’s <em>splendor nimius</em> makes <em>ipsum lumen lucernae vacillabat</em>, the very lamplight falter — Cupid outshines the flame that revealed him.\"",
