 "context": [
  {
   "h": "A description like a painting",
   "body": "<p>This section is an ecphrasis: a detailed description of a work of art, or of something seen as if it were one. Apuleius describes Cupid as a painter would show him, from his golden hair down to his body and the weapons at the foot of the bed. Readers would have known images of Eros as a beautiful winged youth from statues, wall paintings and mosaics, and Apuleius invites them to see him through Psyche's eyes.</p>"
  }
